---
title: 'Series Fills'
---

AG Charts supports fill gradients and fill patterns, providing additional customisation for series and markers.

## Fill Types

Supported Fill Types include:

-   **Solid Fill**: A single CSS colour (#rgb, #rrggbb, rgb(r, g, b), rgba(r, g, b, a), CSS colour name such as 'white', 'orange', 'cyan', etc.)

-   **Gradient Fill**: A transition between multiple colours.

-   **Pattern Fill**: Predefined patterns including lines and shapes.

## Customisation

{% chartExampleRunner title="Fill Types" name="series-fill-types" type="generated" /%}

#### Configuring Series Fill

The `fill` attribute is set at the series level. Solid fills use a CSS colour string. Gradients and patterns require an object with type `gradient` or `pattern`.

```js
series: [
    // ...
    fill: {
        type: 'gradient'
    }
]
```

#### Configuring Marker Fills

[Markers](./markers) in series such as `line` and `area` support the same fill options as series.

The `fill` attribute is contained in the `marker` property of the `series` options.

```js
series: [
    // ...
    marker: {
        fill: {
            type: 'gradient'
        },
    },
]
```

The legend item marker can be modified within the [Legend Options](./legend/#markers).

### Gradients

{% chartExampleRunner title="Gradient Fill" name="gradient-fill" type="generated" /%}

Gradient `colorStops` define an array of colours that transition from one colour to another.

The array should contain a minimum of two objects, each object can define:

-   `color`: Any valid CSS colour value e.g., `red`, `#ff0000`, or `rgb(255,0,0)`.
-   `stop`: A ratio between `0` and `1` indicating the position of the colour along the gradient. `0` is the start of the gradient, and `1` is the end of the gradient.

```js
{
    series: {
        fill: {
            type: 'gradient',
            colorStops: [
                { color: '#A9D4E6', stop: 0 },
                { color: '#5D7FAF', stop: 0.5 },
                { color: '#6A8FD8' }
            ]
        },
    },
}
```

In this configuration:

-   Each colour stops at the `stop` value, and the next colour begins at that point.
-   If no `stop` is provided, the fills will be distributed equally.
-   The last colour is used until the end of the gradient scale.

Please see the [Gradient API reference](#reference-AgGradientColor) for the list of all available options.

### Patterns

{% chartExampleRunner title="Pattern Fill" name="pattern-fill" type="generated" /%}

The following predefined patterns are available:

-   `vertical-lines`
-   `horizontal-lines`
-   `forward-slanted-lines`
-   `backward-slanted-lines`
-   `squares`
-   `circles`
-   `triangles`
-   `diamonds`
-   `stars`
-   `hearts`
-   `crosses`

These can be applied using the `fill.pattern` property.

```js
{
    series: {
        fill: {
            type: 'pattern',
            pattern: 'stars'
        },
    },
}
```

Styling properties such as `stroke`, `strokeWidth`, `backgroundFill` and `fillOpacity` can be used to further customise the patterns.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Pattern Fill Customisation" name="pattern-fill-customisation" type="generated" /%}

Please see the [Pattern API reference](#reference-AgPatternColor) for the list of all available options.

